<title>INDIA: India's GESCO 96/97 1st half net down.</title>
<headline>India's GESCO 96/97 1st half net down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   594.8    vs	737.0</p>
<p>    Income, sales    4,133.0    vs    2,877.8</p>
<p>Gains on sale of</p>
<p>    vessels		Nil	vs	 97.3</p>
<p>    Other income	 105.9    vs	360.1</p>
<p>    Expenditure	2,673.0    vs    1,934.6</p>
<p>    Interest costs     311.0    vs	136.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 572.0    vs	302.7</p>
<p>    Tax		     88.1    vs	224.0</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>Breakup of operating profit</p>
<p>    Shipping	   1,132.0    vs	832.6</p>
<p>    Offshore		55.0    vs	 64.4</p>
<p>Property</p>
<p>    development	  136.0    vs	243.5</p>
<p>    Others		 357.9    vs	360.10</p>
<p>			  --------------------------</p>
<p>			   1,680.9    vs    1,500.6</p>
<p>Less:</p>
<p>Corporate</p>
<p>   administration	115.0    vs	100.0</p>
<p>			  ---------------------------</p>
<p>    Operating profit 1,565.9    vs    1,400.6</p>
<p>Note: Great Eastern Shipping Company Ltd is India's leading private shiping company. It said provision for taxation has been made on the basis of minimum alternate tax and will determine final liability at year end. Figures for the period do not include GAL Offshore, which was subsequently merged with the firm, Great Eastern said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
